~ start
if has_player_won()
	Dealer: Blackjack!
	=> win
% Dealer: Are you going to push your luck?
% Dealer: Why don't you hit!
% Dealer: Stand, if you're afraid of a little risk!
% Dealer: Betting is always fun!
% Dealer: Do it you coward.
% Dealer: How about a little more?
% Dealer: Feeling lucky today?
% Dealer: You need to hit to win!
- Hit
	do hit()
	if has_player_busted()
		% Dealer: What a misfortune, you busted!
		% Dealer: Hit one too many times it seems! What a loss.
		% Dealer: You're clearly not seeing through the cards! What a loss.
		% Dealer: You do know you don't want more than 21 right? You lose!
		% Dealer: That'll do it! You lose.
		% Dealer: Oof, over 21. You lose.
		% Dealer: Too many! You lose.
		=> newgame
	elif has_player_won()
		=> win
	else
		=> start
- Stand
	do stand()
	if who_wins_after_standing()
		=> win
	else
		% Dealer: Should've tried harder! Better luck next time. Loser.
		% Dealer: How unfortunate. You lost.
		% Dealer: Maybe next time will be in your favor? You lose!
		% Dealer: Seems you failed to believe in the heart of the cards!
		=> newgame

~ newgame
% Dealer: Want to play again?
% Dealer: Up for another round?
% Dealer: Let's go again!
% Dealer: Keep playing, won't you?
- Play again [if can_afford_bet() /]
	do ask_bet()
	=> END
- Stop 
	do ask_bet()
	=> END
=> END

~ win
if dealer_helped
	Dealer: *slides you a few extra chips* Don't mention it. Seriously, don't.
% Dealer: Congrats! You win.
% Dealer: You won! Lady luck decided to favor you! 
% Dealer: Congrats, you won! Why not go double or nothing?
% Dealer: Well played, you win! Imagine if you'd bet just a bit more!
% Dealer: Congrats on winning. Blink twice if you marked the cards, I won't tell!
% Dealer: My compliments to the winner!
% Dealer: Congrats on your newfound fortune! You Win!
=> newgame

~ caught
Dealer: Hey! Security!
Guard: Please LEAVE!!!
=> END
